    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 30 tests, 0 failures. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (the `Cp19Tests` acceptance test for this rule already existed and now passes).\n\n**New files:**\n- `CheckOwnerDailyLimit.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (`LocalDate.now()`) and throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count is \u2265 100. It runs before the owner is saved, so the count excludes the owner being created \u2014 mirroring the existing `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` step.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) carrying the date and count.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds with **429 Too Many Requests**.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` \u2014 maps the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `checkDailyLimit` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `checkCityCapacity` and `build`, consistent with the surrounding pre-save validation chain.\n\nThe new function takes only `OwnerRepository` (no `@Val` body needed, since the limit is global by date, not per-request field), and the rule triggers at 100+ owners registered today.",
